</span><span id="alg1.6.11.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:80%;">Rewrite</span><span id="alg1.6.11.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(</span><math id="alg1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s.\mathit{topo}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝑡𝑜𝑝𝑜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s.\mathit{topo}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.11.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">[t])</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.12.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">    </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span id="alg1.6.12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">end parallel for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.13.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><math id="alg1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ok\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ok\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.13.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:80%;">Check</span><span id="alg1.6.13.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(</span><math id="alg1.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(L_{s}.\mathit{out},L_{m}.\mathit{out})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝑜𝑢𝑡</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝑜𝑢𝑡</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L_{s}.\mathit{out},L_{m}.\mathit{out})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.13.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">)</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.14" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.14.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span id="alg1.6.14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">if</span><span id="alg1.6.14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="alg1.6.14.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;"><math id="alg1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ok" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ok</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="alg1.6.14.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.14.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">then</span><span id="alg1.6.14.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.14.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:80%;">PropagateOutputToNextLayer</span><span id="alg1.6.14.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(</span><math id="alg1.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(L_{s}.\mathit{out},L_{m}.\mathit{out})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝑜𝑢𝑡</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝑜𝑢𝑡</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L_{s}.\mathit{out},L_{m}.\mathit{out})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.6.14.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">)</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.15.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span id="alg1.6.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">else</span><span id="alg1.6.15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">return</span><span id="alg1.6.15.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg1.6.15.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">err_abort</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.16" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.10694v1/parallel_rewrite_stages.png" id="S5.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/125;" width="215" height="125" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>. </span><span id="S5.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of the topological traversal.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Once the graphs are divided into different stages, <span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> assigns multiple parallel threads for each stage
(<em id="S5.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</em> <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> in Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.1. Preprocessing: Graph Partitioning and Layer Memoization ‣ 5. System Design ‣ Verifying Computational Graphs in Production-Grade Distributed Machine Learning Frameworks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
Correctness is preserved because the relations computed in each thread depend only on nodes whose inputs have already been analyzed in earlier steps. Dependencies that cross subgraphs are handled naturally by boundary nodes: a boundary node is only rewritten in a later stage once all of its inputs have been resolved in previous stages.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer memoization.</span>
Large models often contain layers with highly similar or identical structures.
Rewriting every such layer independently would repeat the same analysis. To avoid this redundancy,
<span id="S5.SS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> memoizes the results of previously rewritten subgraphs. Each partitioned subgraph is assigned a fingerprint derived from its single-device and distributed forms. When a new subgraph shares the same fingerprint as an earlier one, <span id="S5.SS1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> reuses the memoized relations instead of re-executing the rewriting. Our experience shows this significantly reduces duplicate work across layers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Soundness.</span>
The aforementioned partitioning and memoizations techniques preserve soundness of <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> as a verification tool.
It is possible for <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> to miss rewrite opportunities and relations across partition boundaries such that certain
correct computational graphs cannot be verified, also to re-verify layers that are structurally different but semantically equivalent. However, soundness of <span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> is preserved as the
relation analysis and e-graph rewrite rules are sound.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span>Processing: Incremental E-Graph Construction</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next
we discuss how semantic relations between single-device and distributed graphs are actually established.
Simply applying e-graph rewriting is insufficient: many operators reshape, shard, or merge tensors in ways that require explicit reasoning about their relations.
To handle this, <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> incrementally constructs the e-graph, adding new nodes and relations step by step as it traverses the computation graphs. Each stage of this process activates relation reasoning—starting from input registration, then propagating relations through operators, and extending propagation with bijection inference when the two graphs differ structurally.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.10694v1/full_analysis_example_v2.svg" id="S5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/100;" width="476" height="100"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>. </span><span id="S5.F6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A full computation graph of different reshape, transpose and dot operators with distributed semantics. We show how the partition and layout analysis is integrated with the propagation process (via rule templates defined from Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.2.2. Propagating Relations with Layout and Partition Analysis ‣ 5.2. Processing: Incremental E-Graph Construction ‣ 5. System Design ‣ Verifying Computational Graphs in Production-Grade Distributed Machine Learning Frameworks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
<span id="S5.F6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">S</span> represents shard relations.
<span id="S5.F6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">P</span> represents layout relation of partial tensors.
<math id="S5.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> represents combination of axes. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.1. </span>Registering Input Relations</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The generated graphs from ML compilers by default do not contain information on how the input tensors are related to one another.
<span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> solves this issue by creating relations between graphs by instrumenting compilers and logging sharding/replication information during the IR generation phase. The information is captured as sharding/replication annotations, <em id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</em> <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">shard_along(self, tensor, dim)</span>. These annotations also show the device placement of the distributed tensors.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Certain auxiliary tensors such as those encoding device IDs, <em id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</em> <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torch.arange(tp_degree), sharding=0</span> are not automatically annotated. For these types of information, <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> supplements the missing information by manually specifying which tensors carry device metadata and how they should be interpreted.
These registered input relations serve as the foundation for subsequent reasoning. We discuss how to formally encode these relations in the following subsection.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.2. </span>Propagating Relations with Layout and Partition Analysis</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once input relations are registered, <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> incrementally propagates them through intermediate operators to determine whether the two graphs remain equivalent. This propagation combines several complementary analyses, each addressing different gaps.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F7" class="ltx_figure"><span id="S5.F7.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{@simplebnf_tblr_env}</span>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<p id="S5.F7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.F7.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">[expand=<span id="S5.F7.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">Tensor<math id="S5.F7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></span> <math id="S5.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Coloneqq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⩴</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Coloneqq</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S5.F7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y,z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,z</annotation></semantics></math> baseline tensors
