<br class="ltx_break">       <math id="S5.F7.m267" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ts" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ts</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.F7.4.1.64" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">, <math id="S5.F7.m268" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.F7.m269" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> of baseline slices <math id="S5.F7.m270" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑡𝑠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ts}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.F7.m271" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> lives on rank <math id="S5.F7.m272" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F7.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="S5.F7.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Syntax of relational analysis. We use italics to denote operations and monospace to denote relation symbols.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 5.2.2. Propagating Relations with Layout and Partition Analysis ‣ 5.2. Processing: Incremental E-Graph Construction ‣ 5. System Design ‣ Verifying Computational Graphs in Production-Grade Distributed Machine Learning Frameworks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> gives the relational language that <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> reasons about.
It separates (i) <em id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">objects</em> from (ii) <em id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">operators</em> and (iii) <em id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relations</em>.
Objects include baseline and distributed tensors (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) and layout terms <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> (compose, reshape, transpose, and the <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{bijection}(s_{1},\pi,s_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">bijection</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{bijection}(s_{1},\pi,s_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for a reshape–transpose–reshape triple).
Axes are symbolic (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>) and may combine via <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> to describe mesh products; <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> records an axis correspondence between baseline and distributed views.
Operators summarize only what the analysis needs: element-wise ops, dot, layout application, slicing, and three collectives (all-reduce, all-gather, reduce-scatter).
Relations are the facts <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span> maintains/propagates: <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sharded</span> capture data placement; <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layout</span> records a provably bijective layout transform; <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">partial</span> and the looped <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">loop_red_B</span>/<span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">loop_red_D</span> track per-core partial results that must be discharged by a reduction or collective operation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.2.2. Propagating Relations with Layout and Partition Analysis ‣ 5.2. Processing: Incremental E-Graph Construction ‣ 5. System Design ‣ Verifying Computational Graphs in Production-Grade Distributed Machine Learning Frameworks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lists the Datalog-style rules that drive our analysis.
Rules fall into five families: Partition (propagate sharded), Layout (synthesize/check bijective layouts), Slicing (finer-grained partition), Unroll (handle <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">loop_red_B</span>/<span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">loop_red_D</span>), and a mix of categories above.
We write Datalog-style rules as <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\leftarrow B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\leftarrow B</annotation></semantics></math> (“if <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> holds, derive <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>”). Formally, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, …, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> means conjunction and the rule denotes (<math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}\wedge…\wedge B_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi>…</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}\wedge…\wedge B_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 1</span>. </span><span id="S5.T1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">A subset of Datalog-style analysis rules for partition and layout analysis following the syntax in Figure <a href="#S5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 5.2.2. Propagating Relations with Layout and Partition Analysis ‣ 5.2. Processing: Incremental E-Graph Construction ‣ 5. System Design ‣ Verifying Computational Graphs in Production-Grade Distributed Machine Learning Frameworks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. We additionally use <math id="S5.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leadsto w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↝</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leadsto w</annotation></semantics></math> to mean the sequence of layout transformations. In the actual implementation of <span id="S5.T1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scalify</span>, many rules are polymorphic over operator types.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T1.11" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T1.11.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.11.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Rule</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.11.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.11.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Type</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T1.11.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.11.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.55005pt;"><math id="S5.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{sharded}\left(\textit{elem\_op}\left(x\right),\textit{elem\_op'}\left(x^{\prime}\right),d,c\right)\leftarrow\texttt{sharded}\left(x,x^{\prime},d,c\right),\textit{elem\_op}\left(x\right),\textit{elem\_op'}\left(x^{\prime}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">sharded</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">elem_op</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">elem_op’</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">sharded</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">elem_op</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">elem_op’</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sharded}\left(\textit{elem\_op}\left(x\right),\textit{elem\_op'}\left(x^{\prime}\right),d,c\right)\leftarrow\texttt{sharded}\left(x,x^{\prime},d,c\right),\textit{elem\_op}\left(x\right),\textit{elem\_op'}\left(x^{\prime}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.11.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 2.55005pt;"><span id="S5.T1.11.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Partition</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.11.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.11.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.55005pt;"><math id="S5.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{partial}\left(z,z^{\prime},c,\textit{add}\right)\leftarrow\texttt{sharded}\left(x,x^{\prime},d,c\right),\texttt{sharded}\left(y,y^{\prime},d,c\right),z=\textit{dot}\left(x,y\right),z^{\prime}=\textit{dot'}\left(x^{\prime},y^{\prime}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">partial</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">add</mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">sharded</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">sharded</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">dot</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">dot’</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{partial}\left(z,z^{\prime},c,\textit{add}\right)\leftarrow\texttt{sharded}\left(x,x^{\prime},d,c\right),\texttt{sharded}\left(y,y^{\prime},d,c\right),z=\textit{dot}\left(x,y\right),z^{\prime}=\textit{dot'}\left(x^{\prime},y^{\prime}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.11.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.55005pt;"><span id="S5.T1.11.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Partition + Layout</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.11.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.11.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S5.T1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{sharded}\left(z,z^{\prime},d,c\right),\texttt{layout}\left(z,z^{\prime},\ell^{\prime},c\right),\ell^{\prime}=\textsc{bijection\_inference}\left(\ell,x\leadsto w,x^{\prime}\leadsto w^{\prime}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">sharded</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">layout</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.800em">bijection_inference</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">↝</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">w</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">↝</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">w</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{sharded}\left(z,z^{\prime},d,c\right),\texttt{layout}\left(z,z^{\prime},\ell^{\prime},c\right),\ell^{\prime}=\textsc{bijection\_inference}\left(\ell,x\leadsto w,x^{\prime}\leadsto w^{\prime}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.11.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" rowspan="2"><span id="S5.T1.11.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Layout</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.11.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.11.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.55005pt;"><span id="S5.T1.11.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">   
<math id="S5.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\texttt{layout}\left(x,x^{\prime},\ell,c\right),\texttt{sharded}\left(y,y^{\prime},d,c\right),z=\textit{dot}\left(w,y\right),z^{\prime}=\textit{dot'}\left(w^{\prime},y^{\prime}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">layout</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sharded</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">dot</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">dot’</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\texttt{layout}\left(x,x^{\prime},\ell,c\right),\texttt{sharded}\left(y,y^{\prime},d,c\right),z=\textit{dot}\left(w,y\right),z^{\prime}=\textit{dot'}\left(w^{\prime},y^{\prime}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.11.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.11.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.55005pt;"><math id="S5.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{layout}\left(z,x^{\prime},\ell\circ\textit{transpose}\left(\pi\right),c\right)\leftarrow\texttt{layout}\left(x,x^{\prime},\ell,c\right),z=\textit{transpose}\left(x,\pi\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">layout</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">transpose</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">π</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.800em">layout</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.800em">transpose</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">π</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{layout}\left(z,x^{\prime},\ell\circ\textit{transpose}\left(\pi\right),c\right)\leftarrow\texttt{layout}\left(x,x^{\prime},\ell,c\right),z=\textit{transpose}\left(x,\pi\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T1.11.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-bottom: 2.55005pt;"><span id="S5.T1.11.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Layout</span></td></tr>
